    "body": "<!-- final-brief-v2b -->\nCarried over from #104, which was closed with **landed cost per item** still unchecked. PR #132 merged the contract with **placeholder** numbers (₱3,600, target 6, shipping 900 / 150) and said the real ones come in a separate PR. This is that PR.\n\n**Blocks:** #117 (price table in `services/sourcing.js`), #127 (`POOL_TARGET`), #128 (seed at target − 1), #114 (decision with a number), #122 (the reflection's last sentence).\n**Needed by:** Sat Nov 28, so the code can be finished and rehearsed by Sunday.\n\nThe reasoning has to be ours (AI-use policy). Answer in comments, then one PR.\n\n- [ ] **Landed cost per item** (supplier price + international shipping + fees) for a jersey, a hoodie and a tee\n- [ ] **Our sourcing price per category** (`quotedPrice`): landed cost + margin, with the margin in pesos\n- [ ] **Overseas shipping per item, solo vs pooled** (`shippingSolo`, `shippingPooled`) per category\n- [ ] **`POOL_TARGET`** and why that number (e.g. the order size where pooled shipping beats solo by enough to cover our margin)\n- [ ] **The decision with a number** for 4.4 / free shipping: our real margin on an item, so ₱5,000 stays or moves (#114)\n- [ ] PR: numbers + one-line reasons into `docs/business.md`; replace the placeholder example in `docs/routes.md`; tell #117 and #127 the final constants",
